<title>UK: UK has no immediate plans to privatise Mail-Clarke.</title>
<headline>UK has no immediate plans to privatise Mail-Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday the government had no immediate plans to privatise Britain's remaining major state-owned enterprises.</p>
<p>&quot;We have very few straightforward candidates left for privatisation,&quot; Clarke told reporters after a speech in London. He noted that the Royal Mail and London Underground remained state-owned, but added: &quot;We have no proposals for those at the moment.&quot;</p>
<p>In July, a newspaper said the ruling Conservatives had revived controversial plans to privatise the Post Office and would include the proposals in their election manifesto.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
